PODFoam: NumPy owns each snapshot; calls into Python are checked

The earlier code gave snapshot_func a view of a C++ buffer that the next step
overwrites. The shipped module keeps the first snapshot of each window and so
read the second step's values twice. Each snapshot is now an array NumPy owns,
filled after U and p pass a finite check. A failed import, missing function,
exception or SystemExit stops the run with the traceback. So does an svd_func
result that is not finite float64 with 1 or more columns, or whose count differs
between ranks. Mode files are dimensionless zeroGradient fields. podTruncation
in controlDict, default 5, caps the modes written; more columns give one
warning. The case folder comes first on sys.path. Py_FinalizeEx at exit waits
for non-daemon threads. A changed cell count stops the run. A write step with no
snapshot since the last SVD now collects one; the earlier code ran svd_func at
every write step.

